## Publication checklist

Before publishing measured results from the real branch:

- pin model, dataset, tokenizer, TRL, Transformers, PEFT, Accelerate, and PyTorch revisions;
- report the number of pairs retained, filtered, and truncated;
- split by prompt and add generator/domain slices;
- report pair accuracy, log loss, Brier score, and a calibration plot;
- save LoRA adapters **and** the scalar score head;
- state the T4 type, wall-clock time, peak allocated memory, and random seeds;
- do not present UltraFeedback Binarized as direct human preference data;
- evaluate fresh responses from a policy that was not used to construct the training pairs.
